6-0-0": -10000, "cage-isolated-7-0-0": -10000, "cage-quarantine-5-0-0": -1000, "cage-quarantine-6-0-0": -1000, "cage-quarantine-7-0-0": -1000, "cage-restricted-5-0-0": -100, "cage-restricted-6-0-0": -100, "cage-restricted-7-0-0": -100}, "ceiling": "the sidecar the cage injects at a hardened rung is a stand-in built from platform's own graded/waf-placeholder at the tag this repo pins. Running here means the caged workload started with the sidecar the cage added, not that a real WAF inspected anything.", "fall_closed_namespace": "cage-probe-fallclosed", "fall_closed_priority": -10000, "lowest_cage_priority": -10000, "networkpolicies_selecting_the_fall_closed_pod": ["cage-reach-isolated policyTypes=['Egress', 'Ingress'] ingress=0 egress=0"], "observed": true, "pod": {"caged": "true", "containers": ["app", "waf-sidecar"], "containers_waiting": [], "images": {"app": "ghcr.io/acme/coraza-waf:cage", "waf-sidecar": "ghcr.io/acme/coraza-waf:cage"}, "labels": {"policy-as-versioned.dev/policy-version": "7.0.0", "posture.acme.io/caged": "true", "posture.acme.io/tier": "isolated", "posture.acme.io/version": "7.0.0"}, "namespace": "cage-probe-fallclosed", "phase": "Running", "priority": -10000, "priority_class": "cage-isolated-7-0-0", "ready": true, "scheduled": "True", "scheduling_reason": "", "tier": "isolated", "waiting_reasons": []}, "policy_version_in_force": "7.0.0", "probe_image": "ghcr.io/acme/coraza-waf:cage", "reference_namespace": "cage-probe-reference", "scope": "the cage in force", "why": "the workload the cage put on its bottom rung (isolated) was ADMITTED and is Running, on priority class cage-isolated-7-0-0 (priority -10000, the lowest `cage-` PriorityClass on this cluster), carrying 2 container(s) including waf-sidecar injected by the cage"}, "fact_7_the_bottom_rung_reaches_nothing_while_the_reference_reaches": {"cage_priorityclasses": {"cage-baseline-5-0-0": -10, "cage-baseline-6-0-0": -10, "cage-baseline-7-0-0": -10, "cage-isolated": -10000, "cage-isolated-5-0-0": -10000, "cage-isolated-6-0-0": -10000, "cage-isolated-7-0-0": -10000, "cage-quarantine-5-0-0": -1000, "cage-quarantine-6-0-0": -1000, "cage-quarantine-7-0-0": -1000, "cage-restricted-5-0-0": -100, "cage-restricted-6-0-0": -100, "cage-restricted-7-0-0": -100}, "ceiling": "two pods in two namespaces, not one pod twice: in this cage the rung is a property of the NAMESPACE (ADR-0022) and never of the pod, so the reference cannot be the same workload. The reference is OUTSIDE the cage, so this fact compares the bottom rung with no cage at all: it shows that the bottom rung reaches nothing on a network that works, and it says nothing about the rungs between. Two TCP connects on two ports each -- the API server's ClusterIP and one address outside the cluster -- is not a proof that nothing at all is reachable. Reach is graded on the four connection results and the reference, never on a NetworkPolicy; the NetworkPolicy that selects the bottom-rung pod is read for one purpose only, its rule count is half of the bottom check. The reference brackets the cage's reads rather than running simultaneously with them, so an outage entirely contained between two working reference reads is still unobservable here; it is narrower than one read, not zero.", "fall_closed": {"1.1.1.1:80": "could not connect to 1.1.1.1:80 from cage-probe-fallclosed on 4 reads spanning 9s of held silence", "10.96.0.1:443": "could not connect to 10.96.0.1:443 from cage-probe-fallclosed on 4 reads spanning 9s of held silence"}, "fall_closed_namespace": "cage-probe-fallclosed", "fall_closed_priority": -10000, "fall_closed_tier": "isolated", "lowest_cage_priority": -10000, "networkpolicies_selecting_the_fall_closed_pod": ["cage-reach-isolated policyTypes=['Egress', 'Ingress'] ingress=0 egress=0"], "networkpolicies_selecting_the_reference_pod": [], "observed": true, "policy_version_in_force": "7.0.0", "probe_image": "ghcr.io/acme/coraza-waf:cage", "reference_after": {"1.1.1.1:80": "connected to 1.1.1.1:80 from cage-probe-reference", "10.96.0.1:443": "connected to 10.96.0.1:443 from cage-probe-reference"}, "reference_before": {"1.1.1.1:80": "connected to 1.1.1.1:80 from cage-probe-reference", "10.96.0.1:443": "connected to 10.96.0.1:443 from cage-probe-reference"}, "reference_caged": "", "reference_namespace": "cage-probe-reference", "reference_tier": "", "scope": "the cage in force", "seconds_waited_for_the_cage": 18, "silence_reads_per_target": 4, "targets": ["10.96.0.1:443", "1.1.1.1:80"], "why": "the workload the cage put on its bottom rung (isolated) reached NEITHER the API server nor 1.1.1.1 on 4 reads per target spanning 18s, while the reference workload, which the cage did not select, reached both from the same cluster with the same image BEFORE and AFTER -- a connection refused by the cage, not a YAML read. The rung is the ladder's bottom by priority (-10000, the lowest `cage-` PriorityClass on this cluster) and by a reach policy with no rules"}}, "falsifiers": {"cluster_side_verification_passes_a_tag_that_identity_pinned_ci_rejects": {"ci_accepts": true, "ci_pinned_identity": {"issuer": "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com", "regexp": "^https://github\\.com/policy-as-versioned-nist/nist/\\.github/workflows/cut-release\\.yml@refs/heads/(main|release/[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.x)$"}, "fired": false, "id": "cluster_side_verification_passes_a_tag_that_identity_pinned_ci_rejects", "why": "gitsign verify-tag v1.1.0 accepted the tag against the identity release.yml pins"}, "verified_source_ready_but_the_object_is_absent_or_unequal_and_unhealed": {"fired": null, "id": "verified_source_ready_but_the_object_is_absent_or_unequal_and_unhealed", "kustomization_intervals": ["5m"], "objects_absent_or_unequal": [], "source_ready": true, "why": "unhealed is a property of consecutive samples; `five-facts.py grade` fires this one by walking the log against the live intervals above"}}, "kind": "flux.five-facts/v1", "party": "nist", "pin": {"commit": "33a05df1f5241bca6ffbc1c69a70075c